RecoverSSM GDN commit, bit-identical to per-token decoding: backport of commit 514102a of vllm-project/vllm#58863
(open upstream; by Juergen Schmied, suggested by @ArtyomITA). The verify kernel records the decay it multiplied by,
exp(g), instead of g, and the commit replays the accepted tokens forward with the same update,
h = fma(c, k, h * decay), instead of the closed form s0 * decay + corr. The committed recurrent state is then the
per-token state bit for bit. Same cost: n loads of c, k and the decay.

